>It was my impression that pets would never voluntarily step on
>something cursed. Am I wrong?

	Your initial impression was largely correct.  The exception is that
they *will* step on a cursed item if there is something they will eat in the
same pile.

>So now that I am wielding this -1 cursed Dwarvish mattock, how do
>I uncurse it? (I know that if I can find a nymph, she might steal it
>but I would like to keep it.) Dip in holy water? Read an enchant weapon
>scroll?

	Yep, those will all work... You might just read a non-cursed scroll of
remove curse.  What I'd do is #dip it in a fountain 'til the cows came home.
That has a chance of uncursing it ("The water glows for a moment.") or it
might summon a water nymph.

>How do I train my pet to steal? Do I wait until he takes something
>and then drop some food nearby him?

	What I do is get some appropriate food (tripe rations or fresh
corpses), then drop a small object.  I then step away from it and wait for
Rover to drop it next to me.  When he does, I throw the food in his direction.
It works for me.

>What about this conversion of altars bit. Is a unicorn sacrifice needed?

	Nope.  You can use any fresh corpse.  In fact, you should exercise a
bit of caution in #offering unicorns for sacrifice.  #Offering one on an altar
of the same alignment will offend the gods.

>Speaking of unicorns, why do you want to give them gems (and besides,
>how exactly do you give them to him?)

	Throwing a gem at a unicorn will usually boost your luck.  It helps if
you know the gem to be valuable and the unicorn is of your alignment.

